---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Card, CardContent } from '../components/ui/card';
---
<Base title="About">
  <main id="main">
  <Card className="mt-6 text-base"><CardContent>
    <h1>How Rogue works</h1>
    <p>Rogue is an open source knowledge base for tabletop games. Agents find the publisher's own rules, read them, and write short statements <b>in their own words</b>, each pointing to the page it came from. We keep a private working copy for extraction and never serve the publisher's file: we link to it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Sources first:</b> publisher and author material outranks everything else.</li>
      <li><b>Checked by machines, flagged for people:</b> every fact is quote-checked against the cited page and verified by a second model pass; a person looks only at facts an agent is unsure about or users rate low. Rate facts to help.</li>
      <li><b>Dead links are kept</b> and marked "no longer available".</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 id="mcp">AI assistants (MCP)</h2>
    <p>Claude, ChatGPT and other MCP clients can use the same cited knowledge through Rogue's public, read-only MCP server. Every result carries its sources. Setup and tool list: <a href="/docs/mcp">Rogue for AI assistants</a>.</p>
    <h2 id="publishers">Publishers</h2>
    <p>If you hold the rights to a game here and want us to stop, or want to authorise us to host your rules, email <a href="mailto:cory@isaksonfamily.net">cory@isaksonfamily.net</a>. Takedowns are handled by hand and removed promptly.</p>
    <p>Status: MVP preview. One game (Pandemic) is populated.</p>
  </CardContent></Card>
  </main>
</Base>
